---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Sponsorship & Story Support | Prime Local Growth"
  description="Prime Local Growth helps athletes, families, and personal brands organize their story, prepare sponsorship materials, and approach the right partners."
  path="/sponsorship-marketing"
  ogTitle="Turn your story into better opportunities"
  ogDescription="Sponsorship packages, nomination materials, outreach support, and social-media guidance for athletes and personal brands."
  scripts={["site-interactions", "exit-intent"]}
  stickyAudit={false}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <a class="breadcrumb" href="/">Home</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Sponsorship &amp; story support</p>
      <h1>Make it easier for the right people to understand your value.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Prime Local Growth helps athletes, families, and personal brands turn real accomplishments into clear materials, better outreach, and stronger opportunities.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:adam@primelocalgrowth.com?subject=Sponsorship%20support">Talk about your opportunity</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/results">See the work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <h2>Being good at something is not the same as presenting it well.</h2>
        <p class="sub">Families and growing personal brands often have the results, photos, schedule, and audience. What they lack is a clear story that a sponsor, committee, or partner can understand quickly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>We help organize the pieces.</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>What has been accomplished</li>
          <li>What is coming next</li>
          <li>Who the audience is</li>
          <li>Why a partner is a natural fit</li>
          <li>What the partner receives in return</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we can do</p>
      <h2>Practical support from the first draft to the follow-up.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:28px;">
        <article class="card"><h3>Build the story</h3><p>Season summaries, athlete profiles, nomination answers, media kits, and clear talking points that make the work easy to understand.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Prepare the ask</h3><p>Sponsorship packages, partner benefits, placement ideas, personalized letters, and outreach that connects the opportunity to the right brand.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Support the presence</h3><p>Social-media guidance, content direction, result recaps, sponsor mentions, and a simple plan for staying visible throughout the season.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card highlight">
        <p class="eyebrow">Anonymized project story</p>
        <h2>A season became a professional opportunity.</h2>
        <p class="sub"><strong>Starting point:</strong> A family had a young athlete with strong competition results, a full schedule, social content, and a clear need for sponsor support. The information existed, but it was spread across messages, photos, and posts.</p>
        <p class="sub"><strong>Work completed:</strong> We created a season playbook, organized nomination materials, prepared sponsorship proposals, identified brand-fit opportunities, drafted personalized outreach, guided social-media presentation, and helped manage follow-up.</p>
        <p class="sub"><strong>Documented result:</strong> Email records show sponsor interest, a first primary sponsor, and two confirmed sponsors before the season. The project later expanded into updated nomination materials and an organized tournament ledger for future submissions.</p>
        <p class="proof-note">Names, private contact details, school information, and sponsor identities are intentionally omitted. Specific results are shared publicly only with client permission.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap grid grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2>This is growth work, even when it is not Google work.</h2>
        <p class="sub">The common thread is turning good work into discoverable, understandable, measurable opportunities—whether the next action is a phone call, a booking, a nomination, a sponsor conversation, or a referral.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>A good fit if you need help with:</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>A sponsorship package that sounds like you</li>
          <li>A nomination or application that tells the full story</li>
          <li>A professional way to approach potential partners</li>
          <li>A social-media plan that supports the opportunity</li>
          <li>Follow-up that keeps the conversation moving</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:adam@primelocalgrowth.com?subject=Sponsorship%20support" style="margin-top:18px;">Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
